			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⡏⠀⠀",
				569,
				300
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Backfill extension API shims for real-world extension compatibility\n\nExtend the Cocoon extension host with critical VS Code API features that extensions depend on at runtime, bridging gaps exposed by real-world extension usage (Roo-Code, TypeScript, Error Lens, etc.).\n\nKey additions include:\n- **Extension exports backfill**: Capture the `activate()` return value and store it on the registry entry so `vscode.extensions.getExtension(id).exports` resolves to the real public API (e.g., Roo-Code exposing its agent) instead of an empty permissive stub.\n- **Call/Type hierarchy entry points**: Add `prepareCallHierarchy` and `prepareTypeHierarchy` dispatch cases in the language provider handler so hierarchy UI trees populate correctly when a registered provider exists.\n- **Live `workspace.textDocuments`**: Populate the global open-document list from `$acceptModelAdded` notifications and prune on `$acceptModelRemoved`, making `workspace.textDocuments` reflect the real open set rather than being always empty.\n- **`document.willSave` handling**: Subscribe to save notification, run registered `onWillSaveTextDocument` listeners, collect returned `TextEdits`, and forward them to Mountain via `window.applyTextEdits` so format-on-save and organize-imports-on-save work.\n- **Robust `activeTextEditor` stub**: Replace the minimal placeholder with real `setDecorations` (forwards to Mountain for Sky relay), `edit` (collects edits and applies via `window.applyTextEdits`), `insertSnippet` (converts to plain-text edit), `revealRange`, `show`, and a live `selection` that tracks Monaco selection changes via `window.didChangeTextEditorSelection`.\n- **Workspace event stubs**: Add `onWillSaveTextDocument` subscription wiring, plus no-op disposables for `onWillCreateFiles`, `onWillDeleteFiles`, `onWillRenameFiles`, and their `onDid*` counterparts to prevent TypeError on `.dispose()`.\n- **Module interceptor**: Fix import ordering (`CocoonDevLog` moved after the interface imports) and reformat all `CocoonDevLog` calls for consistent multi-line argument layout.\n- **Cleanup**: Remove stale `Source/Generated/RouteManifest` files and all previously compiled `Target/` artifacts (JS + sourcemaps).\n\nThese changes significantly improve extension host API compliance, enabling extensions that previously failed at runtime due to missing shims.",
			"SHA": "f7889a70696500a1535f8f7d130ee985b6116789"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T01:37:09Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1151,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Define gRPC client service DTOs and interfaces\n\nAdd `Types.ts` to `Source/Services/Mountain/gRPC` to formalize the contract between the Cocoon extension host and the Mountain native backend. This file isolates the Impact-TS `Effect`-based interface definitions and request option shapes for Window, Workspace, Command, Secret Storage, and File System domains.\n\nKey additions include:\n- **Option DTOs**: Definitions for `ShowTextDocumentOptions`, `StatusBarItemOptions`, `WebviewPanelOptions`, and `TextEdit` to standardize payload structures for gRPC calls.\n- **Service Interface**: `IMountainGRPCClientService` exposing type-safe methods for native operations (e.g., `showTextDocument`, `createWebviewPanel`, `readFile`) with explicit `Effect.Effect` return types for error handling and composition.\n\nThis change allows consumers to import types without pulling in the full Effect layer or live implementation, improving modularity and enabling strong typing across the Mountain client service layer.",
			"SHA": "bf9d9ffa2b7ce523e656c4e371993466eeb67deb"
		}
